<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN NOV CONSUMER PRICE INDEX UP 9.2 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN NOV CONSUMER PRICE INDEX UP 9.2 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-items consumer price index rose 0.4 percent in November from October after rising 1.0 percent in October, the Central Statistical Service said.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise was 9.2 percent versus October's 9.1 percent.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast a 0.9 percent month-on-month increase and a 9.5 percent year-on-year rise.  </p>
<p>Pct changes:</p>
<p>			 Year/year			     Month/month</p>
<p>			 Nov '96    Oct '96  Nov '95  -  latest  prev</p>
<p>All items	    9.2	   9.1     6.4	   0.4     1.0</p>
<p>Lower income gp    9.3	   9.4     6.1	   0.3     1.0</p>
<p>Middle income gp   9.6	   9.6     6.6	   0.4     0.9</p>
<p>Higher income gp   9.0	   8.8     6.5	   0.4     0.9</p>
<p>Food only	   11.6	  12.4     0.9	   0.0     2.1</p>
<p>Indices:</p>
<p>			 Nov '96   Oct '96   Nov '95</p>
<p>All items	    189.1     188.4     173.2  </p>
<p>Lower income gp    187.5     187.0     171.6 </p>
<p>Middle income gp   192.6     191.9     175.7</p>
<p>Higher income gp   188.6     187.8     173.0</p>
<p>Food only	    218.9     218.8     196.1</p>
<p>(Index base 1990 = 100)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
